# Secrets and credentials

Never commit, stage, paste into README, PR descriptions, issues, or other tracked files:

- `.env`, `.env.local`, and any file matching `.env*` except a placeholder-only `.env.example`
- Values for `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL`, `UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN`, or any other API keys / tokens / passwords
- Real credentials the user pastes in chat — write them only to gitignored local files (e.g. `.env.local`) when asked

Allowed:

- `.env.example` with empty placeholders and comments only (no real tokens)
- Instructions that say where to set env vars (Vercel / Upstash), without pasting secrets

If asked to commit or open a PR:

- Run `git status` / `git diff` and refuse to include env or secret files
- Never use `--force` to add ignored secret files
- If a secret was accidentally staged, unstage it and warn the user

If a secret appears in chat history, do not echo it back into docs or commits. Prefer referring to “your Upstash REST URL/token in `.env.local`”.
